{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/diveoahu/items/9120/", "pk": 9120, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/diveoahu/", "pk": 226, "shortname": "diveoahu", "name": "Dive Oahu", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Wreck & Reef Tour", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 4, "unicode": "Wreck & Reef Tour", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": true, "sold_out_text": "Call to book", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-midnight", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 3.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-midnight", "cutoff_reached_hours": 3.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 4000, "description": "# CERTIFIED DIVING\n\n##Duration\n3-4 Hours\n\n##About\n\nThe best wreck diving experience in Hawaiian waters! Join us on a guided tour of a stunning wreck on the south shore of Oahu followed by a beautiful guided tour of one of Honolulu's favorite reef sites. Start your day with the best diving experience offered on Oahu! \n\n###Wreck locations include the following:  \n\n* The **Sea Tiger** - Hawaii's deepest recreational diving wreck! The 189' Sea Tiger rests in 123 feet of water while the superstructure and deck are at depths of 60-90', offering great diving!\n\n* The **YO-257 & San Pedro** - These two ships lay side by side with about 50 yards between them. The YO-257 rests in 115 feet of water while the superstructure and deck are at depths of 70-90'. The San Pedro is a bit shallower, 65-85'. **This site can experience strong currents and is only dove when conditions are ideal.** \n\n###Specialty long range charters on _Mondays_, _Wednesdays_ and _Saturdays_ include the following: \n\n* The **Ewa Pinnacles & The Navy Tug** - Embark on a guided tour of the *Ewa Pinnacles*, an ancient lava pinnacle formation covered with Hawaiian corals and surrounded by fish in 75-90' deep water. After your surface interval, come with us to the *Nashua*, a Navy tug boat sunk in 2012 as an artificial reef in 65'. \n\n* The **Corsair & Fantasy Reef** - Dive a WWII fighter plane, the *Corsair* that sits in 115' of water in an upright position. The plane was ditched back in 1948 while on a routine mission from Pearl Harbor. The water may be fairly rough and currents can be strong so this Oahu SCUBA dive is conditions permitting. After your surface interval, come with us to *Fantasy Reef*, one of Honolulu's favorite reef sites in 25-50' of water. \n\n* The **LCU Wreck & Fantasy Reef** - Glide along the *LCU Wreck*, an upside down Landing Craft Utility that is surrounded by artificial reef Z-blocks in 75-90' of water. After your surface interval, come with us to *Fantasy Reef*, one of Honolulu's favorite reef sites in 25-50' of water. \n\n* The **Navy Tug & Keehi Pipe** - Come with us to the *Nashua*, a Navy tug boat sunk in 2012 as an artificial reef in 65'. After your surface interval, come with us to *Keehi Pipe*, another of Honolulu's favorite reef sites in 25-40' of water.\n\n#RIDE ALONG\nHave family or friends that just want to ride along? Bring them!\n\n**Enjoy sights such as**:\n* Critically endangered Honu, Hawaii's Green Sea Turtle at fish cleaning stations. \n* Abundant fish, over 21% of the fish you might see are found nowhere else in the world. \n* Dolphins frolicking nearby\n* Humpback whales in the winter. \n\n**This dive includes:** \n• In-Water Guide\n• All premium gear needed\n• Light snack with refreshments\n\n**Want photos or videos of your snorkel experience? Rent a GoPro for or hire a photographer for additional price.**\n\n**_NOT_ Included:** \n• Gratuity for crew\n• Reef Safe Sunscreen\n• Swimwear\n• Towel", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "***You can NOT fly for 24 hours after diving***\n***You must be at the harbor 30 minutes prior to check in***\n\n**Trip Protection**\nMake sure what happens on land doesn't impact your underwater time! Protect yourself with trip protection so you can cancel your tour anytime and for any reason for a full refund less the cost of trip protection and fees! (90% refunded)\n\nLooking for something extra to add on to your charter? Please give us a call at **(808) 922 - 3483** to ask our staff about the following options: \n- Private Guide\n- Photographer \n- Camera Rental  *(GoPro or SeaLife Camera Housing)*\n\n**Long Range Charters**\n\nPlease note that Dive Oahu cannot guarantee that our dive charters will visit the advertised location(s). The ability to participate at specific dive sites is contingent upon factors such as weather/water conditions, minimum passenger requirements, and/or other circumstances beyond our control. In the event of an altered charter location, Dive Oahu will not be held responsible for any expenses or related costs incurred by participants. We strive to provide an enjoyable and safe experience for all our customers, but unforeseen circumstances may necessitate changes to the planned itinerary. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation regarding this matter. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to contact us.", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 30, "headline": "3-4 Hours • Ages 8+", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/diveoahu/items/9120/images/648772/", "pk": 648772, "unicode": "photo